<title>SOUTH KOREA: Hyundai Motor borrows $60 mln in HK.</title>
<headline>Hyundai Motor borrows $60 mln in HK.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's leading carmaker Hyundai Motor Co Ltd said on Tuesday it had borrowed $60 million from Hong Kong-based Banque Indosuez at 0.55 percent over London Interbank Offered Rate (LIBOR).</p>
<p>The car producer said the five-year maturity loan would be used to finance its marketing and advertising efforts in North America and Europe.</p>
</text>
